{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793089214371,"sessionID":"ses_e838fafdfffe3LhjKrXU2o8Kh0","part":{"partID":"prt_17c721673001W3T62JpYDjppvE","sessionID":"ses_e838fafdfffe3LhjKrXU2o8Kh0","messageID":"msg_17c721010001m56nFK90wvpOMW","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d458e96b35a5bd7","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public && L=specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-1017 && sed -n '/ANCHOR:key-questions/,/\\/ANCHOR:key-questions/p' $L/deep-research-strategy.md && echo \"=== registry questions\" && node -e 'const r=require(\"./'$L'/findings-registry.json\"); console.log(JSON.stringify(r.openQuestions,null,1)); console.log(\"NEXT FOCUS:\"); const s=require(\"fs\").readFileSync(\"'$L'/deep-research-strategy.md\",\"utf8\"); console.log(s.split(\"ANCHOR:next-focus\")[1]?.slice(0,400));'"},"output":"<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] Q1. What unset speckit.worktreeBase and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and does anything still create worktrees under .worktrees/ by default?\n- [ ] Q2. What is git 2.50.1's documented fsmonitor daemon lifecycle on macOS, and how do fsmonitor.socketDir, idle shutdown and git fsmonitor--daemon stop behave when the daemon is wedged?\n- [ ] Q3. Is event overload the real cause of the hang, or is there a known daemon deadlock in this git version, for example around --ipc-threads or the cookie-file handshake?\n- [ ] Q4. Which call sites in the repo's hooks and scripts run git without a timeout, and which of them should opt out of fsmonitor?\n- [ ] Q5. What is the safest default: fsmonitor on with worktrees outside the checkout, or fsmonitor off for the main checkout and on per worktree?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n=== registry questions\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"question-1-q1-what-unset-speckit-worktreebase-and-removed-the-reaper-s-daemon-handling-and-\",\n  \"inboxId\": null,\n  \"text\": \"Q1. What unset speckit.worktreeBase and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and does anything still create worktrees under .worktrees/ by default?\",\n  \"origin\": \"legacy-import\",\n  \"source\": \"key-questions\",\n  \"injectedAtIteration\": 0,\n  \"promotedQuestionId\": null,\n  \"addedAtIteration\": 0,\n  \"resolvedAtIteration\": null\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"question-2-q2-what-is-git-2-50-1-s-documented-fsmonitor-daemon-lifecycle-on-macos-and-how-d\",\n  \"inboxId\": null,\n  \"text\": \"Q2. What is git 2.50.1's documented fsmonitor daemon lifecycle on macOS, and how do fsmonitor.socketDir, idle shutdown and git fsmonitor--daemon stop behave when the daemon is wedged?\",\n  \"origin\": \"legacy-import\",\n  \"source\": \"key-questions\",\n  \"injectedAtIteration\": 0,\n  \"promotedQuestionId\": null,\n  \"addedAtIteration\": 0,\n  \"resolvedAtIteration\": null\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"question-3-q3-is-event-overload-the-real-cause-of-the-hang-or-is-there-a-known-daemon-deadl\",\n  \"inboxId\": null,\n  \"text\": \"Q3. Is event overload the real cause of the hang, or is there a known daemon deadlock in this git version, for example around --ipc-threads or the cookie-file handshake?\",\n  \"origin\": \"legacy-import\",\n  \"source\": \"key-questions\",\n  \"injectedAtIteration\": 0,\n  \"promotedQuestionId\": null,\n  \"addedAtIteration\": 0,\n  \"resolvedAtIteration\": null\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"question-4-q4-which-call-sites-in-the-repo-s-hooks-and-scripts-run-git-without-a-timeout-an\",\n  \"inboxId\": null,\n  \"text\": \"Q4. Which call sites in the repo's hooks and scripts run git without a timeout, and which of them should opt out of fsmonitor?\",\n  \"origin\": \"legacy-import\",\n  \"source\": \"key-questions\",\n  \"injectedAtIteration\": 0,\n  \"promotedQuestionId\": null,\n  \"addedAtIteration\": 0,\n  \"resolvedAtIteration\": null\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"question-5-q5-what-is-the-safest-default-fsmonitor-on-with-worktrees-outside-the-checkout-o\",\n  \"inboxId\": null,\n  \"text\": \"Q5. What is the safest default: fsmonitor on with worktrees outside the checkout, or fsmonitor off for the main checkout and on per worktree?\",\n  \"origin\": \"legacy-import\",\n  \"source\": \"key-questions\",\n  \"injectedAtIteration\": 0,\n  \"promotedQuestionId\": null,\n  \"addedAtIteration\": 0,\n  \"resolvedAtIteration\": null\n }\n]\nNEXT FOCUS:\n -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\nQ1. What unset speckit.worktreeBase and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and does anything still create worktrees under .worktrees/ by default?\n\n<!-- /\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] Q1. What unset speckit.worktreeBase and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and does anything still create worktrees under .worktrees/ by default?\n- [ ] Q2. What is git 2.50.1's documented fsmonitor daemon lifecycle on macOS, and how do fsmonitor.socketDir, idle shutdown and git fsmonitor--daemon stop behave when the daemon is wedged?\n- [ ] Q3. Is event overload the real cause of the hang, or is there a known daemon deadlock in this git version, for example around --ipc-threads or the cookie-file handshake?\n- [ ] Q4. Which call sites in the repo's hooks and scripts run git without a timeout, and which of them should opt out of fsmonitor?\n- [ ] Q5. What is the safest default: fsmonitor on with worktrees outside the checkout, or fsmonitor off for the main checkout and on per worktree?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n=== registry questions\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"question-1-q1-what-unset-speckit-worktreebase-and-removed-the-reaper-s-daemon-handling-and-\",\n  \"inboxId\": null,\n  \"text\": \"Q1. What unset speckit.worktreeBase and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and does anything still create worktrees under .worktrees/ by default?\",\n  \"origi