{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793089390443,"sessionID":"ses_e838fafdfffe3LhjKrXU2o8Kh0","part":{"partID":"prt_17c74bb5d002wU034tcGcwLN0u","sessionID":"ses_e838fafdfffe3LhjKrXU2o8Kh0","messageID":"msg_17c74b441001w0b5gi9mYlAcM4","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8549e8f710d70f5","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public && grep -rn --exclude-dir=node_modules --exclude-dir=.worktrees --include='*.sh' --include='*.md' --include='*.cjs' --include='*.json' \"worktree-reaper\" .skilled specs/sk-git 2>/dev/null | grep -v \"/tests/\" | head -15","timeout":90000},"output":".skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh:42:log() { echo \"[worktree-reaper] $*\" >&2; }\n.skilled/bin/README.md:75:+-- worktree-reaper.sh             # Prune merged/clean per-session worktrees + stale socket dirs\n.skilled/bin/README.md:168:| `bash .skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh [--dry-run]` | CLI | Prune merged + clean per-session worktrees, stale socket dirs and session markers. never signals a process. Auto-reap is restricted to proven-inactive exact `work/<runtime>/<slug>` pairs (the whole marker file must match a PID grammar, a malformed marker is treated as ambiguous and the worktree is kept. the branch's runtime/slug must equal the directory basename). |\n.skilled/bin/README.md:235:bash -n .skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/fixtures/phrase-variants.json:115067:      \"worktree-reaper.sh\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/fixtures/corpus-manifest.json:6562:    \".skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/session-lifecycle/worktree-reaper.md\",\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/data/trigger-index.json:1634:    \".skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/session-lifecycle/worktree-reaper.md\",\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md:574:| Worktree isolation | `.skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh` creates a per-session git worktree with isolated `SPEC_KIT_DB_DIR` / `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR`. Pair with `worktree-reaper.sh` for teardown and `worktree-guard.sh` for lock enforcement |\n.skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:85:`worktree-reaper.sh` removes a `work/<runtime>/<slug>` worktree only when all three hold at once: the tree is clean, its branch is merged into the live integration tip (the primary checkout's actual `HEAD`, not a possibly stale local `main`), and its session is proven inactive by a marker file recording a now-dead process id. Detached worktrees, human task worktrees (`worktrees/NNN-slug`), and any wrapper worktree with a missing or unreadable marker are always report-only. The reaper never signals a process.\n.skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:89:See [`session-lifecycle/worktree-reaper.md`](session-lifecycle/worktree-reaper.md) for full implementation and test file listings.\n.skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/session-lifecycle/launch-wrapper-session-isolation.md:66:- [worktree-reaper.md](worktree-reaper.md) — Worktree reaper\n.skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/session-lifecycle/worktree-reaper.md:6:  - \"worktree-reaper.sh\"\n.skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/session-lifecycle/worktree-reaper.md:13:# Worktree reaper (worktree-reaper.sh)\n.skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/session-lifecycle/worktree-reaper.md:45:| `.skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh` | Script | Worktree pruning gate, socket/marker cleanup |\n.skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/session-lifecycle/worktree-reaper.md:59:- Feature file path: `session-lifecycle/worktree-reaper.md`\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh:42:log() { echo \"[worktree-reaper] $*\" >&2; }\n.skilled/bin/README.md:75:+-- worktree-reaper.sh             # Prune merged/clean per-session worktrees + stale socket dirs\n.skilled/bin/README.md:168:| `bash .skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh [--dry-run]` | CLI | Prune merged + clean per-session worktrees, stale socket dirs and session markers. never signals a process. Auto-reap is restricted to proven-inactive exact `work/<runtime>/<slug>` pairs (the whole marker file must match a PID grammar, a malformed marker is treated as ambiguous and the worktree is kept. the branch's runtime/slug must equal the directory basename). |\n.skilled/bin/README.md:235:bash -n .skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/fixtures/phrase-variants.json:115067:      \"worktree-reaper.sh\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/fixtures/corpus-manifest.json:6562:    \".skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/session-lifecycle/worktree-reaper.md\",\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/data/trigger-index.json:1634:    \".skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/session-lifecycle/worktree-reaper.md\",\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md:574:| Worktree isolation | `.skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh` creates a per-session git worktree with isolated `SPEC_KIT_DB_DIR` / `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR`. Pair with `worktree-reaper.sh` for teardown and `worktree-guard.sh` for lock enforcement |\n.skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:85:`worktree-reaper.sh` removes a `work/<runtime>/<slug>` worktree only when all three hold at once: the tree is clean, its branch is merged into the live integration tip (the primary checkout's actual `HEAD`, not a possibly stale local `main`), and its session is proven inactive by a marker file recording a now-dead process id. Detached worktrees, human task worktrees (`worktrees/NNN-slug`), and any wrapper worktree with a missing or unreadable marker are always report-only. The reaper never signals a process.\n.skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:89:See [`session-lifecycle/worktree-reaper.md`](session-lifecycle/worktree-reaper.md) for full implementation and test file listings.\n.skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/session-lifecycle/launch-wrapper-session-isolation.md:66:- [worktree-reaper.md](worktree-reaper.md) — Worktree reaper\n.skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/session-lifecycle/worktree-reaper.md:6:  - \"worktree-reaper.sh\"\n.skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/session-lifecycle/worktree-reaper.md:13:# Worktree reaper (worktree-reaper.sh)\n.skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/session-lifecycle/worktree-reaper.md:45:| `.skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh` | Script | Worktree pruning gate, socket/marker cleanup |\n.skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/session-lifecycle/worktree-reaper.md:59:- Feature file path: `session-lifecycle/worktree-reaper.md`\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public && grep -rn --exclude-dir=node_modules --exclude-dir=.worktrees --include='*.sh' --include='*.md' --include='*.cjs' --include='*.json' \\\"worktree-reaper\\\" .skilled specs/sk-git 2>/dev/null | grep -v \\\"/tests/\\\" | head -15\", \"timeout\": 90000}"},"time":{"start":1793089387357,"end":1793089390443}}}}
