{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1793089398502,"sessionID":"ses_e838fafdfffe3LhjKrXU2o8Kh0","part":{"id":"prt_17c74e6e6001ct3sZGWzJp1UU4","sessionID":"ses_e838fafdfffe3LhjKrXU2o8Kh0","messageID":"msg_17c74e14b001E4Pxi6WoINczdc","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793089404645,"sessionID":"ses_e838fafdfffe3LhjKrXU2o8Kh0","part":{"partID":"prt_17c74e6e7001CRjU0JHoFCu5Gl","sessionID":"ses_e838fafdfffe3LhjKrXU2o8Kh0","messageID":"msg_17c74e14b001E4Pxi6WoINczdc","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-af5866032375c816","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 1: The sk-git/026 regression — who moved the worktrees back and where the reaper's daemon handling went\n\n## Focus\n\nQ1 of the packet's section 8: what unset `speckit.worktreeBase` and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and whether anything still defaults worktrees to `.worktrees/`. This iteration reads the completed sk-git/026 packet, the current worktree scripts, and the git history of the reaper, and re-measures the live daemon population.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Read `specs/sk-git/026-worktree-hygiene-and-relocation/implementation-summary.md` for the recorded outcomes (prune, fsmonitor on, configurable base set to `~/worktrees/public`, reaper \"generalized daemon-orphan detection\").\n2. Read the resolved-base code paths: `.skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh` `_wn_base_dir()`, `.skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh` base resolution and config write-back, `.skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh` header and section list.\n3. Traced the reaper's history with `git log --oneline -- <path>` and `git log -S \"daemon\"` over both the pre-move `.opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh` and the current `.skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh`, then read the full reaper diff of the commit that dropped the daemon block.\n4. Traced the config write-back history with `git log -S 'config speckit.worktreeBase \"$WT_BASE_DIR\"'`.\n5. Re-measured the live state: `git config --show-origin --get-regexp 'fsmonitor|untracked|worktreeBase|extensions'`, `ls -d .worktrees/*`, `ls ~/worktrees`, and a `ps -Ao pid,lstart,command` census of `fsmonitor--daemon run` processes.\n6. Checked `~/.zsh_history` for an `unset speckit.worktreeBase` record (no hit).\n\n## Findings\n\n1. The reaper's daemon handling was deleted by `3c7c3f83874` (2026-09-03, \"refactor(runtime): remove the memory launcher, plugin, hooks and the tool-ownership commit gate\"), not by the `.opencode` → `.skilled` source-root move. That commit removed the `--reap-daemons` flag, the `_daemon_worktree_path_from_cmdline()` and `_daemon_cmdline_is_orphan()` helpers, the whole \"5. ORPHAN DAEMON REPORTING\" block, and the closing `orphan daemon candidates` log line from `.opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh`. [SOURCE: git show 3c7c3f83874 -- .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh]\n\n2. The deleted logic never matched `git fsmonitor--daemon` at all. It enumerated `pgrep -f 'context-server\\.js'` and skipped every process whose command line was not `*node*context-server.js*`, i.e. the retired spec-memory MCP daemons whose lease lived under a worktree DB dir. Two separate daemon populations were conflated in the packet's premise: sk-git/026 reaped MCP context-server daemons, and today's pile-up is git's own fsmonitor daemon. [SOURCE: git show 3c7c3f83874 -- .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh]\n\n3. Restoring \"the reaper's daemon handling\" therefore would not stop a single fsmonitor daemon. A fsmonitor reaper is new work, not a revert. [INFERENCE: from findings 1-2 plus `.skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh` now containing no `daemon`, `fsmonitor` or `orphan` token]\n\n4. `speckit.worktreeBase` is local-only configuration: `git config --show-origin --get-regexp` prints it nowhere for this checkout (only `file:.git/config core.fsmonitor true` and `core.untrackedcache true`), and no commit can unset an unversioned `.git/config` key. The regression was not a code revert of the relocation policy; the policy record simply is not in the repository. [SOURCE: git config --show-origin output, this session]\n\n5. The durable in-checkout default is re-created by the launch wrapper itself. `.skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:292-295` writes `speckit.worktreeBase = $WT_BASE_DIR` whenever the key is unset, and `_wn_base_dir()` falls back to `<toplevel>/.worktrees` when neither `SPECKIT_WORKTREE_BASE` nor the config key exists. So one launch without the env var converts the intended `~/worktrees/public` policy into a permanent `.worktrees` policy. [SOURCE: .skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:292] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh:71]\n\n6. The auto-pin is recent: `f83952c3a94` (2026-09-11, \"fix(sk-git): keep the reaper off live sessions and record autosync rewrites\") introduced the config write-back, three weeks after `a69a621a39a` (2026-08-21) introduced the configurable base. The window between the two commits is exactly when a launch could have re-pinned `.worktrees` without any operator intent. [SOURCE: git log -S 'config speckit.worktreeBase \"$WT_BASE_DIR\"' -- .opencode/bin/worktree-session.sh .skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh]\n\n7. Nothing else in the repo opts this checkout out of the in-checkout default. `.worktrees` is still the documented default in `worktree-naming.sh:13`, `README.md:115`, and `README.md:125`, and the only documented way back out is a manual `git config speckit.worktreeBase <abs>`; the changelog even advertises \"Unset the config to return to the in-checkout `.worktrees` layout\" as a supported action. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh:13] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-git/changelog/v1.5.2.0.md:29]\n\n8. The live state matches the in-checkout default: `git config --get speckit.worktreeBase` is empty, `~/worktrees` exists but is empty, and 13 worktrees sit under `Public/.worktrees/` (087, 103, 140, 144, 145, 156, 197, 216, 217, 218, 219, 230, 231). The empty `~/worktrees` directory is the residue of the relocation, not of a live policy. [SOURCE: ls -d .worktrees/*, this session] [SOURCE: ls -la ~/worktrees, this session]\n\n9. Eleven `git fsmonitor--daemon run --detach --ipc-threads=8` processes are alive as of 09:22Z, the oldest started Oct 11 18:29:55 (PID 1157, 16 days), and every one of them is Xcode's `git-core`. Nothing in the repo starts, stops, or bounds them: the reaper is a manual CLI, and its published invariant is now \"never signals a process\". [SOURCE: ps -Ao pid,lstart,command output, this session] [SOURCE: .skilled/bin/README.md:168]\n\n10. Because the reaper documents \"never signals a process\", re-adding daemon killing inside `worktree-reaper.sh` would break a published contract rather than restore one; a fsmonitor reap belongs in its own entry point (or in a `--reap-fsmonitor` sibling) whose invariant can be stated separately. [SOURCE: .skilled/bin/README.md:168] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:85]\n\n## Questions Answered\n\n- Q1. What unset speckit.worktreeBase and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and does anything still create worktrees under .worktrees/ by default? — Answer: two different events. The reaper's daemon block was deleted by `3c7c3f83874` (2026-09-03) in the memory-launcher refactor, and it only ever targeted MCP `context-server.js` daemons. The base key was not unset by any commit (it is unversioned local config); the launch wrapper re-pins it on any unset launch, defaulting to `.worktrees`. Yes — `.worktrees` remains the code default, all 13 worktrees live there, and 11 fsmonitor daemons persist from Oct 11 onward.\n\n## Questions Remaining\n\n- Q2. Git 2.50.1's documented daemon lifecycle on macOS (idle exit, `fsmonitor.socketDir`, `git fsmonitor--daemon stop` on a wedged daemon).\n- Q3. Event overload versus a known 2.50.1 daemon deadlock (`--ipc-threads`, cookie handshake).\n- Q4. Which hook/script git call sites lack a timeout.\n- Q5. Safest default shape.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- \"The `.opencode` → `.skilled` move removed the daemon handling.\" Ruled out: `git log -S daemon` puts the deletion in `3c7c3f83874`, and the move commit `330427cf308` is the only commit touching the current path.\n- \"A repo commit reverted the relocated worktree base.\" Ruled out: the key is local config; the only repo-side actor is the wrapper's write-back.\n- \"An operator shell command unset it and is recoverable from this shell's history.\" No hit in `~/.zsh_history`; the unset, if manual, happened in another session or before history rotation.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Git-config provenance for `speckit.worktreeBase`: `.git/config` is not versioned, so the exact unset action is unrecoverable from the repository. Recorded as an explicit UNKNOWN rather than guessed.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Contradictory evidence: the packet's own wording calls the removed code \"the reaper's daemon handling\" and the current pile-up \"fsmonitor daemons\", which reads as one lineage of work. The code shows two unrelated daemon families. Resolution: recorded as findings 1-3 rather than smoothed over; the premise correction is load-bearing for the fix design.\n- Missing dependency: no access to the pre-unset `.git/config`; the UNKNOWN stands with the check that would resolve it (a `.git/config` copy in a backup or another clone's config).\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `specs/sk-git/026-worktree-hygiene-and-relocation/implementation-summary.md`\n- `git show 3c7c3f83874 -- .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh`\n- `git log --oneline -S \"daemon\" -- .skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh`\n- `git log --oneline -S 'config speckit.worktreeBase \"$WT_BASE_DIR\"' -- .opencode/bin/worktree-session.sh .skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh`\n- `.skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:219,292-295`\n- `.skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh`\n- `.skilled/bin/README.md:168`\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh:13,61-83`\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-git/README.md:115,125`\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-git/changelog/v1.5.2.0.md:21,29`\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:85`\n- `ps -Ao pid,lstart,command | grep [f]smonitor--daemon run` (11 processes)\n- `git config --show-origin --get-regexp \"fsmonitor|untracked|worktreeBase|extensions\"`\n- `ls -d .worktrees/*`, `ls -la ~/worktrees`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.85\n- Questions addressed: Q1\n- Questions answered: Q1\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: `git log -S` over both path spellings, then reading the full diff of the one commit that matched, converted a vague \"the reaper lost something\" into an exact deletion with a date and a reason. Re-measuring the live process census in the same session kept the fourteen-day-old daemon observation current instead of inherited.\n- What did not work and why: chasing config provenance through git history was structurally impossible — the key is unversioned. Reading the wrapper's write-back found the real persistence mechanism instead.\n- What I would do differently: start from the code path that writes the key (write-back) rather than from \"who unset it\", because an unset that is silently re-pinned is a different bug from an unset that stays unset.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nQ2 and Q3 together: git 2.50.1's fsmonitor daemon lifecycle on macOS — whether a daemon can exit on its own, what `fsmonitor.socketDir`, idle shutdown and `git fsmonitor--daemon stop` do, and whether `--ipc-threads=8` or the cookie handshake has a known wedge in this version. The `--ipc-threads=8` argument in every live process is not something this repo passes, so its origin and its deadlock surface need an authoritative answer.\n","path":"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-1017/iterations/iteration-001.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-1017/iterations/iteration-001.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-1017/iterations/iteration-001.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 1: The sk-git/026 regression — who moved the worktrees back and where the reaper's daemon handling went\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nQ1 of the packet's section 8: what unset `speckit.worktreeBase` and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and whether anything still defaults worktrees to `.worktrees/`. This iteration reads the completed sk-git/026 packet, the current worktree scripts, and the git history of the reaper, and re-measures the live daemon population.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n1. Read `specs/sk-git/026-worktree-hygiene-and-relocation/implementation-summary.md` for the recorded outcomes (prune, fsmonitor on, configurable base set to `~/worktrees/public`, reaper \\\"generalized daemon-orphan detection\\\").\\n2. Read the resolved-base code paths: `.skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh` `_wn_base_dir()`, `.skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh` base resolution and config write-back, `.skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh` header and section list.\\n3. Traced the reaper's history with `git log --oneline -- <path>` and `git log -S \\\"daemon\\\"` over both the pre-move `.opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh` and the current `.skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh`, then read the full reaper diff of the commit that dropped the daemon block.\\n4. Traced the config write-back history with `git log -S 'config speckit.worktreeBase \\\"$WT_BASE_DIR\\\"'`.\\n5. Re-measured the live state: `git config --show-origin --get-regexp 'fsmonitor|untracked|worktreeBase|extensions'`, `ls -d .worktrees/*`, `ls ~/worktrees`, and a `ps -Ao pid,lstart,command` census of `fsmonitor--daemon run` processes.\\n6. Checked `~/.zsh_history` for an `unset speckit.worktreeBase` record (no hit).\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. The reaper's daemon handling was deleted by `3c7c3f83874` (2026-09-03, \\\"refactor(runtime): remove the memory launcher, plugin, hooks and the tool-ownership commit gate\\\"), not by the `.opencode` → `.skilled` source-root move. That commit removed the `--reap-daemons` flag, the `_daemon_worktree_path_from_cmdline()` and `_daemon_cmdline_is_orphan()` helpers, the whole \\\"5. ORPHAN DAEMON REPORTING\\\" block, and the closing `orphan daemon candidates` log line from `.opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh`. [SOURCE: git show 3c7c3f83874 -- .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh]\\n\\n2. The deleted logic never matched `git fsmonitor--daemon` at all. It enumerated `pgrep -f 'context-server\\\\.js'` and skipped every process whose command line was not `*node*context-server.js*`, i.e. the retired spec-memory MCP daemons whose lease lived under a worktree DB dir. Two separate daemon populations were conflated in the packet's premise: sk-git/026 reaped MCP context-server daemons, and today's pile-up is git's own fsmonitor daemon. [SOURCE: git show 3c7c3f83874 -- .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh]\\n\\n3. Restoring \\\"the reaper's daemon handling\\\" therefore would not stop a single fsmonitor daemon. A fsmonitor reaper is new work, not a revert. [INFERENCE: from findings 1-2 plus `.skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh` now containing no `daemon`, `fsmonitor` or `orphan` token]\\n\\n4. `speckit.worktreeBase` is local-only configuration: `git config --show-origin --get-regexp` prints it nowhere for this checkout (only `file:.git/config core.fsmonitor true` and `core.untrackedcache true`), and no commit can unset an unversioned `.git/config` key. The regression was not a code revert of the relocation policy; the policy record simply is not in the repository. [SOURCE: git config --show-origin output, this session]\\n\\n5. The durable in-checkout default is re-created by the launch wrapper itself. `.skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:292-295` writes `speckit.worktreeBase = $WT_BASE_DIR` whenever the key is unset, and `_wn_base_dir()` falls back to `<toplevel>/.worktrees` when neither `SPECKIT_WORKTREE_BASE` nor the config key exists. So one launch without the env var converts the intended `~/worktrees/public` policy into a permanent `.worktrees` policy. [SOURCE: .skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:292] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh:71]\\n\\n6. The auto-pin is recent: `f83952c3a94` (2026-09-11, \\\"fix(sk-git): keep the reaper off live sessions and record autosync rewrites\\\") introduced the config write-back, three weeks after `a69a621a39a` (2026-08-21) introduced the configurable base. The window between the two commits is exactly when a launch could have re-pinned `.worktrees` without any operator intent. [SOURCE: git log -S 'config speckit.worktreeBase \\\"$WT_BASE_DIR\\\"' -- .opencode/bin/worktree-session.sh .skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh]\\n\\n7. Nothing else in the repo opts this checkout out of the in-checkout default. `.worktrees` is still the documented default in `worktree-naming.sh:13`, `README.md:115`, and `README.md:125`, and the only documented way back out is a manual `git config speckit.worktreeBase <abs>`; the changelog even advertises \\\"Unset the config to return to the in-checkout `.worktrees` layout\\\" as a supported action. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh:13] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-git/changelog/v1.5.2.0.md:29]\\n\\n8. The live state matches the in-checkout default: `git config --get speckit.worktreeBase` is empty, `~/worktrees` exists but is empty, and 13 worktrees sit under `Public/.worktrees/` (087, 103, 140, 144, 145, 156, 197, 216, 217, 218, 219, 230, 231). The empty `~/worktrees` directory is the residue of the relocation, not of a live policy. [SOURCE: ls -d .worktrees/*, this session] [SOURCE: ls -la ~/worktrees, this session]\\n\\n9. Eleven `git fsmonitor--daemon run --detach --ipc-threads=8` processes are alive as of 09:22Z, the oldest started Oct 11 18:29:55 (PID 1157, 16 days), and every one of them is Xcode's `git-core`. Nothing in the repo starts, stops, or bounds them: the reaper is a manual CLI, and its published invariant is now \\\"never signals a process\\\". [SOURCE: ps -Ao pid,lstart,command output, this session] [SOURCE: .skilled/bin/README.md:168]\\n\\n10. Because the reaper documents \\\"never signals a process\\\", re-adding daemon killing inside `worktree-reaper.sh` would break a published contract rather than restore one; a fsmonitor reap belongs in its own entry point (or in a `--reap-fsmonitor` sibling) whose invariant can be stated separately. [SOURCE: .skilled/bin/README.md:168] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:85]\\n\\n## Questions Answered\\n\\n- Q1. What unset speckit.worktreeBase and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and does anything still create worktrees under .worktrees/ by default? — Answer: two different events. The reaper's daemon block was deleted by `3c7c3f83874` (2026-09-03) in the memory-launcher refactor, and it only ever targeted MCP `context-server.js` daemons. The base key was not unset by any commit (it is unversioned local config); the launch wrapper re-pins it on any unset launch, defaulting to `.worktrees`. Yes — `.worktrees` remains the code default, all 13 worktrees live there, and 11 fsmonitor daemons persist from Oct 11 onward.\\n\\n## Questions Remaining\\n\\n- Q2. Git 2.50.1's documented daemon lifecycle on macOS (idle exit, `fsmonitor.socketDir`, `git fsmonitor--daemon stop` on a wedged daemon).\\n- Q3. Event overload versus a known 2.50.1 daemon deadlock (`--ipc-threads`, cookie handshake).\\n- Q4. Which hook/script git call sites lack a timeout.\\n- Q5. Safest default shape.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- \\\"The `.opencode` → `.skilled` move removed the daemon handling.\\\" Ruled out: `git log -S daemon` puts the deletion in `3c7c3f83874`, and the move commit `330427cf308` is the only commit touching the current path.\\n- \\\"A repo commit reverted the relocated worktree base.\\\" Ruled out: the key is local config; the only repo-side actor is the wrapper's write-back.\\n- \\\"An operator shell command unset it and is recoverable from this shell's history.\\\" No hit in `~/.zsh_history`; the unset, if manual, happened in another session or before history rotation.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Git-config provenance for `speckit.worktreeBase`: `.git/config` is not versioned, so the exact unset action is unrecoverable from the repository. Recorded as an explicit UNKNOWN rather than guessed.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Contradictory evidence: the packet's own wording calls the removed code \\\"the reaper's daemon handling\\\" and the current pile-up \\\"fsmonitor daemons\\\", which reads as one lineage of work. The code shows two unrelated daemon families. Resolution: recorded as findings 1-3 rather than smoothed over; the premise correction is load-bearing for the fix design.\\n- Missing dependency: no access to the pre-unset `.git/config`; the UNKNOWN stands with the check that would resolve it (a `.git/config` copy in a backup or another clone's config).\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `specs/sk-git/026-worktree-hygiene-and-relocation/implementation-summary.md`\\n- `git show 3c7c3f83874 -- .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh`\\n- `git log --oneline -S \\\"daemon\\\" -- .skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh`\\n- `git log --oneline -S 'config speckit.worktreeBase \\\"$WT_BASE_DIR\\\"' -- .opencode/bin/worktree-session.sh .skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh`\\n- `.skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:219,292-295`\\n- `.skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh`\\n- `.skilled/bin/README.md:168`\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh:13,61-83`\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-git/README.md:115,125`\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-git/changelog/v1.5.2.0.md:21,29`\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:85`\\n- `ps -Ao pid,lstart,command | grep [f]smonitor--daemon run` (11 processes)\\n- `git config --show-origin --get-regexp \\\"fsmonitor|untracked|worktreeBase|extensions\\\"`\\n- `ls -d .worktrees/*`, `ls -la ~/worktrees`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.85\\n- Questions addressed: Q1\\n- Questions answered: Q1\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: `git log -S` over both path spellings, then reading the full diff of the one commit that matched, converted a vague \\\"the reaper lost something\\\" into an exact deletion with a date and a reason. Re-measuring the live process census in the same session kept the fourteen-day-old daemon observation current instead of inherited.\\n- What did not work and why: chasing config provenance through git history was structurally impossible — the key is unversioned. Reading the wrapper's write-back found the real persistence mechanism instead.\\n- What I would do differently: start from the code path that writes the key (write-back) rather than from \\\"who unset it\\\", because an unset that is silently re-pinned is a different bug from an unset that stays unset.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nQ2 and Q3 together: git 2.50.1's fsmonitor daemon lifecycle on macOS — whether a daemon can exit on its own, what `fsmonitor.socketDir`, idle shutdown and `git fsmonitor--daemon stop` do, and whether `--ipc-threads=8` or the cookie handshake has a known wedge in this version. The `--ipc-threads=8` argument in every live process is not something this repo passes, so its origin and its deadlock surface need an authoritative answer.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-1017/iterations/iteration-001.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793089398503,"end":1793089404645}}}}
