{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1793089407807,"sessionID":"ses_e838fafdfffe3LhjKrXU2o8Kh0","part":{"id":"prt_17c750b3f001KfJHPUAcqX7hGE","sessionID":"ses_e838fafdfffe3LhjKrXU2o8Kh0","messageID":"msg_17c7503dd001JH5Xx7OYmEvgsy","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793089412280,"sessionID":"ses_e838fafdfffe3LhjKrXU2o8Kh0","part":{"partID":"prt_17c750e23002QPGT8narYCIQyh","sessionID":"ses_e838fafdfffe3LhjKrXU2o8Kh0","messageID":"msg_17c7503dd001JH5Xx7OYmEvgsy","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e902d202503293a","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":1,\"run\":1,\"runId\":\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-1017-1793088864734-4s5169\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-1017-1793088864734-4s5169\",\"lineageId\":\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-1017-1793088864734-4s5169\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"newInfoRatio\":0.85,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"The sk-git/026 regression: who moved the worktrees back and where the reaper's daemon handling went\",\"findingsCount\":10,\"noveltyJustification\":\"Nine of ten findings are new to the packet: the deletion commit, the MCP-versus-fsmonitor family correction, the wrapper config write-back, and the live census were all unrecorded.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Q1. What unset speckit.worktreeBase and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and does anything still create worktrees under .worktrees/ by default?\",\"Q2. What is git 2.50.1's documented fsmonitor daemon lifecycle on macOS, and how do fsmonitor.socketDir, idle shutdown and git fsmonitor--daemon stop behave when the daemon is wedged?\",\"Q3. Is event overload the real cause of the hang, or is there a known daemon deadlock in this git version, for example around --ipc-threads or the cookie-file handshake?\",\"Q4. Which call sites in the repo's hooks and scripts run git without a timeout, and which of them should opt out of fsmonitor?\",\"Q5. What is the safest default: fsmonitor on with worktrees outside the checkout, or fsmonitor off for the main checkout and on per worktree?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"Q1. What unset speckit.worktreeBase and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and does anything still create worktrees under .worktrees/ by default?\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"The .opencode to .skilled move removed the daemon handling\",\"A repo commit reverted the relocated worktree base\",\"The unset is recoverable from this shell's history\"],\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Grep\",\"Bash\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\"specs/sk-git/026-worktree-hygiene-and-relocation/implementation-summary.md\",\"git show 3c7c3f83874 -- .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh\",\"git log -S daemon -- .skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh\",\"git log -S config speckit.worktreeBase -- .opencode/bin/worktree-session.sh .skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh\",\".skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:292\",\".skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh\",\".skilled/bin/README.md:168\",\".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh:71\",\".skilled/skills/sk-git/changelog/v1.5.2.0.md:29\",\"ps -Ao pid,lstart,command\",\"git config --show-origin --get-regexp\",\".worktrees/\",\"~/worktrees\"],\"edgeCase\":\"contradictory-evidence\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-27T08:23:15Z\",\"durationMs\":0,\"graphEvents\":[{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"q1-base-and-reaper\",\"kind\":\"QUESTION\",\"label\":\"What unset the worktree base and removed the reaper daemon handling\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-reaper-deleted-by-memory-refactor\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"Reaper daemon block deleted by commit 3c7c3f83874\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-mcp-vs-fsmonitor\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"Removed logic targeted MCP context-server daemons, never git fsmonitor\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-wrapper-repins-base\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"Launch wrapper writes speckit.worktreeBase back on every unset launch\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-q1-1\",\"source\":\"f-reaper-deleted-by-memory-refactor\",\"target\":\"q1-base-and-reaper\",\"relation\":\"ANSWERS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-q1-2\",\"source\":\"f-mcp-vs-fsmonitor\",\"target\":\"f-reaper-deleted-by-memory-refactor\",\"relation\":\"CONTRADICTS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-q1-3\",\"source\":\"f-wrapper-repins-base\",\"target\":\"q1-base-and-reaper\",\"relation\":\"ANSWERS\"}]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-001\",\"label\":\"Commit 3c7c3f83874 (2026-09-03) deleted the reaper's --reap-daemons flag, the _daemon_worktree_path_from_cmdline and _daemon_cmdline_is_orphan helpers, and the whole ORPHAN DAEMON REPORTING block from .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"git show 3c7c3f83874 -- .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-002\",\"label\":\"The deleted reaper logic only enumerated pgrep -f context-server.js and skipped any command line not matching *node*context-server.js*, so it targeted retired spec-memory MCP daemons and never matched git fsmonitor--daemon.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"git show 3c7c3f83874 -- .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh\",\".skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-003\",\"label\":\"Restoring the reaper's daemon handling would not stop a single fsmonitor daemon; a fsmonitor reaper is new work rather than a revert.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\".skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh\",\".skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:85\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-004\",\"label\":\"speckit.worktreeBase is unversioned local config: no commit can unset it, and this checkout currently has no such key set, so the relocation policy record simply is not in the repository.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"git config --show-origin --get-regexp fsmonitor|untracked|worktreeBase|extensions\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-005\",\"label\":\".skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:292-295 writes speckit.worktreeBase whenever the key is unset, and _wn_base_dir() defaults to <toplevel>/.worktrees, so one launch without SPECKIT_WORKTREE_BASE re-pins the in-checkout base permanently.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\".skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:292\",\".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh:71\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-006\",\"label\":\"The auto-pin arrived in f83952c3a94 (2026-09-11), three weeks after a69a621a39a (2026-08-21) introduced the configurable base, opening a window where a launch re-pinned .worktrees with no operator intent.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"git log -S config speckit.worktreeBase -- .opencode/bin/worktree-session.sh .skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-007\",\"label\":\"The in-checkout default is still documented as the default in worktree-naming.sh:13 and README.md:115,125, and the changelog advertises unsetting the config as the supported way back to .worktrees.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh:13\",\".skilled/skills/sk-git/README.md:125\",\".skilled/skills/sk-git/changelog/v1.5.2.0.md:29\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-008\",\"label\":\"Live state matches the in-checkout default: no speckit.worktreeBase, an empty ~/worktrees, and 13 worktrees under Public/.worktrees (087, 103, 140, 144, 145, 156, 197, 216, 217, 218, 219, 230, 231).\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\".worktrees/\",\"~/worktrees\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-009\",\"label\":\"Eleven git fsmonitor--daemon run --detach --ipc-threads=8 processes were alive at 09:22Z, the oldest from Oct 11 18:29:55 (PID 1157), all from Xcode git-core, and nothing in the repo starts, bounds or stops them.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"ps -Ao pid,lstart,command\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-010\",\"label\":\"worktree-reaper.sh is a manual CLI whose published invariant is now never signals a process, so daemon killing must move to a separate entry point instead of being re-added to it.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\".skilled/bin/README.md:168\",\".skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:85\"]}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"The .opencode to .skilled source-root move removed the reaper's daemon handling\",\"reason\":\"git log -S daemon places the deletion in 3c7c3f83874, and the move commit 330427cf308 only renamed the path.\",\"iteration\":1}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"A repository commit reverted the relocated worktree base\",\"reason\":\"The key is unversioned .git/config; the only repo-side writer is the worktree-session.sh write-back.\",\"iteration\":1}\n","path":"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-1017/deltas/iter-001.jsonl"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-1017/deltas/iter-001.jsonl","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-1017/deltas/iter-001.jsonl"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"{\\\"type\\\":\\\"iteration\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":1,\\\"run\\\":1,\\\"runId\\\":\\\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-1017-1793088864734-4s5169\\\",\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-1017-1793088864734-4s5169\\\",\\\"lineageId\\\":\\\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-1017-1793088864734-4s5169\\\",\\\"mode\\\":\\\"research\\\",\\\"target_agent\\\":\\\"deep-research\\\",\\\"agent_definition_loaded\\\":true,\\\"resolved_route\\\":\\\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\\\",\\\"newInfoRatio\\\":0.85,\\\"status\\\":\\\"complete\\\",\\\"focus\\\":\\\"The sk-git/026 regression: who moved the worktrees back and where the reaper's daemon handling went\\\",\\\"findingsCount\\\":10,\\\"noveltyJustification\\\":\\\"Nine of ten findings are new to the packet: the deletion commit, the MCP-versus-fsmonitor family correction, the wrapper config write-back, and the live census were all unrecorded.\\\",\\\"keyQuestions\\\":[\\\"Q1. What unset speckit.worktreeBase and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and does anything still create worktrees under .worktrees/ by default?\\\",\\\"Q2. What is git 2.50.1's documented fsmonitor daemon lifecycle on macOS, and how do fsmonitor.socketDir, idle shutdown and git fsmonitor--daemon stop behave when the daemon is wedged?\\\",\\\"Q3. Is event overload the real cause of the hang, or is there a known daemon deadlock in this git version, for example around --ipc-threads or the cookie-file handshake?\\\",\\\"Q4. Which call sites in the repo's hooks and scripts run git without a timeout, and which of them should opt out of fsmonitor?\\\",\\\"Q5. What is the safest default: fsmonitor on with worktrees outside the checkout, or fsmonitor off for the main checkout and on per worktree?\\\"],\\\"answeredQuestions\\\":[\\\"Q1. What unset speckit.worktreeBase and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and does anything still create worktrees under .worktrees/ by default?\\\"],\\\"ruledOut\\\":[\\\"The .opencode to .skilled move removed the daemon handling\\\",\\\"A repo commit reverted the relocated worktree base\\\",\\\"The unset is recoverable from this shell's history\\\"],\\\"toolsUsed\\\":[\\\"Read\\\",\\\"Grep\\\",\\\"Bash\\\"],\\\"sourcesQueried\\\":[\\\"specs/sk-git/026-worktree-hygiene-and-relocation/implementation-summary.md\\\",\\\"git show 3c7c3f83874 -- .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh\\\",\\\"git log -S daemon -- .skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh\\\",\\\"git log -S config speckit.worktreeBase -- .opencode/bin/worktree-session.sh .skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh\\\",\\\".skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:292\\\",\\\".skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh\\\",\\\".skilled/bin/README.md:168\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh:71\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/sk-git/changelog/v1.5.2.0.md:29\\\",\\\"ps -Ao pid,lstart,command\\\",\\\"git config --show-origin --get-regexp\\\",\\\".worktrees/\\\",\\\"~/worktrees\\\"],\\\"edgeCase\\\":\\\"contradictory-evidence\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-10-27T08:23:15Z\\\",\\\"durationMs\\\":0,\\\"graphEvents\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"q1-base-and-reaper\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"QUESTION\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"What unset the worktree base and removed the reaper daemon handling\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-reaper-deleted-by-memory-refactor\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"FINDING\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Reaper daemon block deleted by commit 3c7c3f83874\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-mcp-vs-fsmonitor\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"FINDING\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Removed logic targeted MCP context-server daemons, never git fsmonitor\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-wrapper-repins-base\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"FINDING\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Launch wrapper writes speckit.worktreeBase back on every unset launch\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"edge\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"e-q1-1\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"f-reaper-deleted-by-memory-refactor\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"q1-base-and-reaper\\\",\\\"relation\\\":\\\"ANSWERS\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"edge\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"e-q1-2\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"f-mcp-vs-fsmonitor\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"f-reaper-deleted-by-memory-refactor\\\",\\\"relation\\\":\\\"CONTRADICTS\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"edge\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"e-q1-3\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"f-wrapper-repins-base\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"q1-base-and-reaper\\\",\\\"relation\\\":\\\"ANSWERS\\\"}]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter001-001\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Commit 3c7c3f83874 (2026-09-03) deleted the reaper's --reap-daemons flag, the _daemon_worktree_path_from_cmdline and _daemon_cmdline_is_orphan helpers, and the whole ORPHAN DAEMON REPORTING block from .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":1,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"git show 3c7c3f83874 -- .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter001-002\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The deleted reaper logic only enumerated pgrep -f context-server.js and skipped any command line not matching *node*context-server.js*, so it targeted retired spec-memory MCP daemons and never matched git fsmonitor--daemon.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":1,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"git show 3c7c3f83874 -- .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh\\\",\\\".skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter001-003\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Restoring the reaper's daemon handling would not stop a single fsmonitor daemon; a fsmonitor reaper is new work rather than a revert.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":1,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:85\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter001-004\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"speckit.worktreeBase is unversioned local config: no commit can unset it, and this checkout currently has no such key set, so the relocation policy record simply is not in the repository.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":1,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"git config --show-origin --get-regexp fsmonitor|untracked|worktreeBase|extensions\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter001-005\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\".skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:292-295 writes speckit.worktreeBase whenever the key is unset, and _wn_base_dir() defaults to <toplevel>/.worktrees, so one launch without SPECKIT_WORKTREE_BASE re-pins the in-checkout base permanently.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":1,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:292\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh:71\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter001-006\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The auto-pin arrived in f83952c3a94 (2026-09-11), three weeks after a69a621a39a (2026-08-21) introduced the configurable base, opening a window where a launch re-pinned .worktrees with no operator intent.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":1,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"git log -S config speckit.worktreeBase -- .opencode/bin/worktree-session.sh .skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter001-007\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The in-checkout default is still documented as the default in worktree-naming.sh:13 and README.md:115,125, and the changelog advertises unsetting the config as the supported way back to .worktrees.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":1,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh:13\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/sk-git/README.md:125\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/sk-git/changelog/v1.5.2.0.md:29\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter001-008\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Live state matches the in-checkout default: no speckit.worktreeBase, an empty ~/worktrees, and 13 worktrees under Public/.worktrees (087, 103, 140, 144, 145, 156, 197, 216, 217, 218, 219, 230, 231).\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":1,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".worktrees/\\\",\\\"~/worktrees\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter001-009\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Eleven git fsmonitor--daemon run --detach --ipc-threads=8 processes were alive at 09:22Z, the oldest from Oct 11 18:29:55 (PID 1157), all from Xcode git-core, and nothing in the repo starts, bounds or stops them.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":1,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"ps -Ao pid,lstart,command\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter001-010\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"worktree-reaper.sh is a manual CLI whose published invariant is now never signals a process, so daemon killing must move to a separate entry point instead of being re-added to it.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":1,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/bin/README.md:168\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:85\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"ruled_out\\\",\\\"direction\\\":\\\"The .opencode to .skilled source-root move removed the reaper's daemon handling\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"git log -S daemon places the deletion in 3c7c3f83874, and the move commit 330427cf308 only renamed the path.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":1}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"ruled_out\\\",\\\"direction\\\":\\\"A repository commit reverted the relocated worktree base\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The key is unversioned .git/config; the only repo-side writer is the worktree-session.sh write-back.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":1}\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-1017/deltas/iter-001.jsonl\"}"},"time":{"start":1793089408547,"end":1793089412280}}}}
