{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793089432595,"sessionID":"ses_e838fafdfffe3LhjKrXU2o8Kh0","part":{"partID":"prt_17c75696a001PJIzgWtCg4L9HL","sessionID":"ses_e838fafdfffe3LhjKrXU2o8Kh0","messageID":"msg_17c75583d001It2aubcaSFg3uq","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c5dfa113a775c4a","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public && (man -P cat git-fsmonitor--daemon 2>/dev/null | sed -n '1,120p') || echo \"NO_LOCAL_MANPAGE\"; echo \"=== config docs local\"; (man -P cat git-config 2>/dev/null | grep -n -A6 -i \"fsmonitor.socketDir\\|core.fsmonitor\" | head -40) || true"},"output":"GIT-FSMONITOR--DAEMON(1)          Git Manual          GIT-FSMONITOR--DAEMON(1)\n\nN\bNA\bAM\bME\bE\n     git-fsmonitor--daemon - A Built-in Filesystem Monitor\n\nS\bSY\bYN\bNO\bOP\bPS\bSI\bIS\bS\n     _\bg_\bi_\bt _\bf_\bs_\bm_\bo_\bn_\bi_\bt_\bo_\br_\b-_\b-_\bd_\ba_\be_\bm_\bo_\bn start\n     _\bg_\bi_\bt _\bf_\bs_\bm_\bo_\bn_\bi_\bt_\bo_\br_\b-_\b-_\bd_\ba_\be_\bm_\bo_\bn run\n     _\bg_\bi_\bt _\bf_\bs_\bm_\bo_\bn_\bi_\bt_\bo_\br_\b-_\b-_\bd_\ba_\be_\bm_\bo_\bn stop\n     _\bg_\bi_\bt _\bf_\bs_\bm_\bo_\bn_\bi_\bt_\bo_\br_\b-_\b-_\bd_\ba_\be_\bm_\bo_\bn status\n\nD\bDE\bES\bSC\bCR\bRI\bIP\bPT\bTI\bIO\bON\bN\n     A daemon to watch the working directory for file and directory changes\n     using platform-specific filesystem notification facilities.\n\n     This daemon communicates directly with commands like g\bgi\bit\bt s\bst\bta\bat\btu\bus\bs using the\n     s\bsi\bim\bmp\bpl\ble\be I\bIP\bPC\bC[1] interface instead of the slower g\bgi\bit\bth\bho\boo\bok\bks\bs(5) interface.\n\n     This daemon is built into Git so that no third-party tools are required.\n\nO\bOP\bPT\bTI\bIO\bON\bNS\bS\n     start\n         Starts a daemon in the background.\n\n     run\n         Runs a daemon in the foreground.\n\n     stop\n         Stops the daemon running in the current working directory, if\n         present.\n\n     status\n         Exits with zero status if a daemon is watching the current working\n         directory.\n\nR\bRE\bEM\bMA\bAR\bRK\bKS\bS\n     This daemon is a long running process used to watch a single working\n     directory and maintain a list of the recently changed files and\n     directories. Performance of commands such as g\bgi\bit\bt s\bst\bta\bat\btu\bus\bs can be increased\n     if they just ask for a summary of changes to the working directory and\n     can avoid scanning the disk.\n\n     When c\bco\bor\bre\be.\b.f\bfs\bsm\bmo\bon\bni\bit\bto\bor\br is set to t\btr\bru\bue\be (see g\bgi\bit\bt-\b-c\bco\bon\bnf\bfi\big\bg(1)) commands, such as\n     g\bgi\bit\bt s\bst\bta\bat\btu\bus\bs, will ask the daemon for changes and automatically start it\n     (if necessary).\n\n     For more information see the \"File System Monitor\" section in g\bgi\bit\bt-\b-u\bup\bpd\bda\bat\bte\be-\b-\n     i\bin\bnd\bde\bex\bx(1).\n\nC\bCA\bAV\bVE\bEA\bAT\bTS\bS\n     The fsmonitor daemon does not currently know about submodules and does\n     not know to filter out filesystem events that happen within a submodule.\n     If fsmonitor daemon is watching a super repo and a file is modified\n     within the working directory of a submodule, it will report the change\n     (as happening against the super repo). However, the client will properly\n     ignore these extra events, so performance may be affected but it will not\n     cause an incorrect result.\n\n     By default, the fsmonitor daemon refuses to work with network-mounted\n     repositories; this may be overridden by setting f\bfs\bsm\bmo\bon\bni\bit\bto\bor\br.\b.a\bal\bll\blo\bow\bwR\bRe\bem\bmo\bot\bte\be to\n     t\btr\bru\bue\be. Note, however, that the fsmonitor daemon is not guaranteed to work\n     correctly with all network-mounted repositories, so such use is\n     considered experimental.\n\n     On Mac OS, the inter-process communication (IPC) between various Git\n     commands and the fsmonitor daemon is done via a Unix domain socket (UDS)\n     — a special type of file — which is supported by native Mac OS\n     filesystems, but not on network-mounted filesystems, NTFS, or FAT32.\n     Other filesystems may or may not have the needed support; the fsmonitor\n     daemon is not guaranteed to work with these filesystems and such use is\n     considered experimental.\n\n     By default, the socket is created in the .g\bgi\bit\bt directory. However, if the\n     .g\bgi\bit\bt directory is on a network-mounted filesystem, it will instead be\n     created at $\b$H\bHO\bOM\bME\bE/\b/.\b.g\bgi\bit\bt-\b-f\bfs\bsm\bmo\bon\bni\bit\bto\bor\br-\b-*\b* unless $\b$H\bHO\bOM\bME\bE itself is on a\n     network-mounted filesystem, in which case you must set the configuration\n     variable f\bfs\bsm\bmo\bon\bni\bit\bto\bor\br.\b.s\bso\boc\bck\bke\bet\btD\bDi\bir\br to the path of a directory on a Mac OS\n     native filesystem in which to create the socket file.\n\n     If none of the above directories (.g\bgi\bit\bt, $\b$H\bHO\bOM\bME\bE, or f\bfs\bsm\bmo\bon\bni\bit\bto\bor\br.\b.s\bso\boc\bck\bke\bet\btD\bDi\bir\br) is\n     on a native Mac OS file filesystem the fsmonitor daemon will report an\n     error that will cause the daemon and the currently running command to\n     exit.\n\nC\bCO\bON\bNF\bFI\bIG\bGU\bUR\bRA\bAT\bTI\bIO\bON\bN\n     Everything below this line in this section is selectively included from\n     the g\bgi\bit\bt-\b-c\bco\bon\bnf\bfi\big\bg(1) documentation. The content is the same as what’s found\n     there:\n\n     fsmonitor.allowRemote\n         By default, the fsmonitor daemon refuses to work with network-mounted\n         repositories. Setting f\bfs\bsm\bmo\bon\bni\bit\bto\bor\br.\b.a\bal\bll\blo\bow\bwR\bRe\bem\bmo\bot\bte\be to t\btr\bru\bue\be overrides this\n         behavior. Only respected when c\bco\bor\bre\be.\b.f\bfs\bsm\bmo\bon\bni\bit\bto\bor\br is set to t\btr\bru\bue\be.\n\n     fsmonitor.socketDir\n         This Mac OS-specific option, if set, specifies the directory in which\n         to create the Unix domain socket used for communication between the\n         fsmonitor daemon and various Git commands. The directory must reside\n         on a native Mac OS filesystem. Only respected when c\bco\bor\bre\be.\b.f\bfs\bsm\bmo\bon\bni\bit\bto\bor\br is\n         set to t\btr\bru\bue\be.\n\nG\bGI\bIT\bT\n     Part of the g\bgi\bit\bt(1) suite\n\nN\bNO\bOT\bTE\bES\bS\n      1. simple IPC\n         git-htmldocs/technical/api-simple-ipc.html\n\nGit 2.50.1.428.g0e8243            2025-07-22          GIT-FSMONITOR--DAEMON(1)\n=== config docs local\n1924:     core.fsmonitor\n1925-         If set to true, enable the built-in file system monitor daemon for\n1926-         this working directory (g\bgi\bit\bt-\b-f\bfs\bsm\bmo\bon\bni\bit\bto\bor\br-\b--\b-d\bda\bae\bem\bmo\bon\bn(1)).\n1927-\n1928-         Like hook-based file system monitors, the built-in file system\n1929-         monitor can speed up Git commands that need to refresh the Git index\n1930-         (e.g.  g\bgi\bit\bt s\bst\bta\bat\btu\bus\bs) in a working directory with many files. The\n--\n1960:     core.fsmonitorHookVersion\n1961-         Sets the protocol version to be used when invoking the \"fsmonitor\"\n1962-         hook.\n1963-\n1964-         There are currently versions 1 and 2. When this is not set, version 2\n1965-         will be tried first and if it fails then version 1 will be tried.\n1966-         Version 1 uses a timestamp as input to determine which files have\n--\n3550:     fsmonitor.socketDir\n3551-         This Mac OS-specific option, if set, specifies the directory in which\n3552-         to create the Unix domain socket used for communication between the\n3553-         fsmonitor daemon and various Git commands. The directory must reside\n3554-         on a native Mac OS filesystem. Only respected when c\bco\bor\bre\be.\b.f\bfs\bsm\bmo\bon\bni\bit\bto\bor\br is\n3555-         set to t\btr\bru\bue\be.\n3556-\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"GIT-FSMONITOR--DAEMON(1)          Git Manual          GIT-FSMONITOR--DAEMON(1)\n\nN\bNA\bAM\bME\bE\n     git-fsmonitor--daemon - A Built-in Filesystem Monitor\n\nS\bSY\bYN\bNO\bOP\bPS\bSI\bIS\bS\n     _\bg_\bi_\bt _\bf_\bs_\bm_\bo_\bn_\bi_\bt_\bo_\br_\b-_\b-_\bd_\ba_\be_\bm_\bo_\bn start\n     _\bg_\bi_\bt _\bf_\bs_\bm_\bo_\bn_\bi_\bt_\bo_\br_\b-_\b-_\bd_\ba_\be_\bm_\bo_\bn run\n     _\bg_\bi_\bt _\bf_\bs_\bm_\bo_\bn_\bi_\bt_\bo_\br_\b-_\b-_\bd_\ba_\be_\bm_\bo_\bn stop\n     _\bg_\bi_\bt _\bf_\bs_\bm_\bo_\bn_\bi_\bt_\bo_\br_\b-_\b-_\bd_\ba_\be_\bm_\bo_\bn status\n\nD\bDE\bES\bSC\bCR\bRI\bIP\bPT\bTI\bIO\bON\bN\n     A daemon to watch the working directory for file and directory changes\n     using platform-specific filesystem notification facilities.\n\n     This daemon communicates directly with commands like g\bgi\bit\bt s\bst\bta\bat\btu\bus\bs using the\n     s\bsi\bim\bmp\bpl\ble\be I\bIP\bPC\bC[1] interface instead of the slower g\bgi\bit\bth\bho\boo\bok\bks\bs(5) interface.\n\n     This daemon is built into Git so that no third-party tools are required.\n\nO\bOP\bPT\bTI\bIO\bON\bNS\bS\n     start\n         Starts a daemon in the background.\n\n     run\n         Runs a daemon in the foreground.\n\n     stop\n         Stops the daemon running in the current working directory, if\n         present.\n\n     status\n         Exits with zero status if a daemon is watching the current working\n         directory.\n\nR\bRE\bEM\bMA\bAR\bRK\bKS\bS\n     This daemon is a long running process used to watch a single working\n     directory and maintain a list of the recently changed files and\n     directories. Performance of commands such as g\bgi\bit\bt s\bst\bta\bat\btu\bus\bs can be increased\n     if they just ask for a summary of changes to the working directory and\n     can avoid scanning the disk.\n\n     When c\bco\bor\bre\be.\b.f\bfs\bsm\bmo\bon\bni\bit\bto\bor\br is set to t\btr\bru\bue\be (see g\bgi\bit\bt-\b-c\bco\bon\bnf\bfi\big\bg(1)) commands, such as\n     g\bgi\bit\bt s\bst\bta\bat\btu\bus\bs, will ask the daemon for changes and automatically start it\n     (if necessary).\n\n     For more information see the \"File System Monitor\" section in g\bgi\bit\bt-\b-u\bup\bpd\bda\bat\bte\be-\b-\n     i\bin\bnd\bde\bex\bx(1).\n\nC\bCA\bAV\bVE\bEA\bAT\bTS\bS\n     The fsmonitor daemon does not currently know about submodules and does\n     not know to filter out filesystem events that happen within a submodule.\n     If fsmonitor daemon is watching a super repo and a file is modified\n     within the working directory of a submodule, it will report the change\n     (as happening against the super repo). However, the client will properly\n     ignore these extra events, so performance may be affected but it will not\n     cause an incorrect result.\n\n     By default, the fsmonitor daemon refuses to work with network-mounted\n     repositories; this may be overridden by setting f\bfs\bsm\bmo\bon\bni\bit\bto\bor\br.\b.a\bal\bll\blo\bow\bwR\bRe\bem\bmo\bot\bte\be to\n     t\btr\bru\bue\be. Note, however, that the fsmonitor daemon is not guaranteed to work\n     correctly with all network-mounted repositories, so such use is\n     considered experimental.\n\n     On Mac OS, the inter-process communication (IPC) between various Git\n     commands and the fsmonitor daemon is done via a Unix domain socket (UDS)\n     — a special type of file — which is supported by native Mac OS\n     filesystems, but not on network-mounted filesystems, NTFS, or FAT32.\n     Other filesystems may or may not have the needed support; the fsmonitor\n     daemon is not guaranteed to work with these filesystems and such use is\n     considered experimental.\n\n     By default, the socket is created in the .g\bgi\bit\bt directory. However, if the\n     .g\bgi\bit\bt directory is on a network-mounted filesystem, it will instead be\n     created at $\b$H\bHO\bOM\bME\bE/\b/.\b.g\bgi\bit\bt-\b-f\bfs\bsm\bmo\bon\bni\bit\bto\bor\br-\b-*\b* unless $\b$H\bHO\bOM\bME\bE itself is on a\n     network-mounted filesystem, in which case you must set the configuration\n     variable f\bfs\bsm\bmo\bon\bni\bit\bto\bor\br.\b.s\bso\boc\bck\bke\bet\btD\bDi\bir\br to the path of a directory on a Mac OS\n     native filesystem in which to create the socket file.\n\n     If none of the above directories (.g\bgi\bit\bt, $\b$H\bHO\bOM\bME\bE, or f\bfs\bsm\bmo\bon\bni\bit\bto\bor\br.\b.s\bso\boc\bck\bke\bet\btD\bDi\bir\br) is\n     on a native Mac OS file filesystem the fsmonitor daemon will report an\n     error that will cause the daemon and the currently running command to\n     exit.\n\nC\bCO\bON\bNF\bFI\bIG\bGU\bUR\bRA\bAT\bTI\bIO\bON\bN\n     Everything below this line in this section is selectively included from\n     the g\bgi\bit\bt-\b-c\bco\bon\bnf\bfi\big\bg(1) documentation. The content is the same as what’s found\n     there:\n\n     fsmonitor.allowRemote\n         By default, the fsmonitor daemon refuses to work with network-mounted\n         repositories. Setting f\bfs\bsm\bmo\bon\bni\bit\bto\bor\br.\b.a\bal\bll\blo\bow\bwR\bRe\bem\bmo\bot\bte\be to t\btr\bru\bue\be overrides this\n         behavior. Only respected when c\bco\bor\bre\be.\b.f\bfs\bsm\bmo\bon\bni\bit\bto\bor\br is set to t\btr\bru\bue\be.\n\n     fsmonitor.socketDir\n         This Mac OS-specific option, if set, specifies the directory in which\n         to create the Unix domain socket used for communication between the\n         fsmonitor daemon and various Git commands. The directory must reside\n         on a native Mac OS filesystem. Only respected when c\bco\bor\bre\be.\b.f\bfs\bsm\bmo\bon\bni\bit\bto\bor\br is\n         set to t\btr\bru\bue\be.\n\nG\bGI\bIT\bT\n     Part of the g\bgi\bit\bt(1) suite\n\nN\bNO\bOT\bTE\bES\bS\n      1. simple IPC\n         git-htmldocs/technical/api-simple-ipc.html\n\nGit 2.50.1.428.g0e8243            2025-07-22          GIT-FSMONITOR--DAEMON(1)\n=== config docs local\n1924:     core.fsmonitor\n1925-         If set to true, enable the built-in file system monitor daemon for\n1926-         this working directory (g\bgi\bit\bt-\b-f\bfs\bsm\bmo\bon\bni\bit\bto\bor\br-\b--\b-d\bda\bae\bem\bmo\bon\bn(1)).\n1927-\n1928-         Like hook-based file system monitors, the built-in file system\n1929-         monitor can speed up Git commands that need to refresh the Git index\n1930-         (e.g.  g\bgi\bit\bt s\bst\bta\bat\btu\bus\bs) in a working directory with many files. The\n--\n1960:     core.fsmonitorHookVersion\n1961-         Sets the protocol version to be used when invoking the \"fsmonitor\"\n1962-         hook.\n1963-\n1964-         There are currently versions 1 and 2. When this is not set, version 2\n1965-         will be tried first and if it fails then version 1 will be tried.\n1966-         Version 1 uses a timestamp as input to determine which files have\n--\n3550:     fsmonitor.socketDir\n3551-         This Mac OS-specific option, if set, specifies the directory in which\n3552-         to create the Unix domain socket used for communication between the\n3553-         fsmonitor daemon and various Git commands. The directory must reside\n3554-         on a native Mac OS filesystem. Only respected when c\bco\bor\bre\be.\b.f\bfs\bsm\bmo\bon\bni\bit\bto\bor\br is\n3555-         set to t\btr\bru\bue\be.\n3556-\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public && (man -P cat git-fsmonitor--daemon 2>/dev/null | sed -n '1,120p') || echo \\\"NO_LOCAL_MANPAGE\\\"; echo \\\"=== config docs local\\\"; (man -P cat git-config 2>/dev/null | grep -n -A6 -i \\\"fsmonitor.socketDir\\\\|core.fsmonitor\\\" | head -40) || true\"}"},"time":{"start":1793089431914,"end":1793089432595}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793089433648,"sessionID":"ses_e838fafdfffe3LhjKrXU2o8Kh0","part":{"partID":"prt_17c756a32001ja9aWlRneWTKBY","sessionID":"ses_e838fafdfffe3LhjKrXU2o8Kh0","messageID":"msg_17c75583d001It2aubcaSFg3uq","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ff2070d1cd2b5c7","tool":"webfetch","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"url":"https://git-scm.com/docs/git-fsmonitor--daemon","format":"markdown"},"output":"[![Git](/images/logo@2x.png)](/)\n\n![](/images/dark-mode.svg)\n\n- [About](/about)\n\n  - [Trademark](/about/trademark)\n\n- [Learn](/learn)\n\n  - [Book](/book)\n\n  - [Cheat Sheet](/cheat-sheet)\n\n  - [Videos](/videos)\n\n  - [External Links](/doc/ext)\n\n- [Tools](/tools)\n\n  - [Command Line](/tools/command-line)\n\n  - [GUIs](/tools/guis)\n\n  - [Hosting](/tools/hosting)\n\n- [Reference](/docs)\n\n- [Install](/install)\n\n- [Community](/community)\n\n- Table of Contents\n\n  - [NAME](#_name)\n\n  - [SYNOPSIS](#_synopsis)\n\n  - [DESCRIPTION](#_description)\n\n  - [OPTIONS](#_options)\n\n  - [REMARKS](#_remarks)\n\n  - [CAVEATS](#_caveats)\n\n  - [CONFIGURATION](#_configuration)\n\n  - [GIT](#_git)\n\n[ English ▾](#)\n\nLocalized versions of **git-fsmonitor--daemon** manual\n\n1. [English](/docs/git-fsmonitor--daemon)\n\nWant to read in your language or fix typos?  \n[You can help translate this page](https://github.com/jnavila/git-manpages-l10n).\n\n[Topics ▾](#)\n\n### Setup and Config\n\n- [ git](/docs/git)\n\n- [ config](/docs/git-config)\n\n- [ help](/docs/git-help)\n\n- [ bugreport](/docs/git-bugreport)\n\n- [ Credential helpers](/doc/credential-helpers)\n\n### Getting and Creating Projects\n\n- [ init](/docs/git-init)\n\n- [ clone](/docs/git-clone)\n\n### Basic Snapshotting\n\n- [ add](/docs/git-add)\n\n- [ status](/docs/git-status)\n\n- [ diff](/docs/git-diff)\n\n- [ commit](/docs/git-commit)\n\n- [ notes](/docs/git-notes)\n\n- [ restore](/docs/git-restore)\n\n- [ reset](/docs/git-reset)\n\n- [ rm](/docs/git-rm)\n\n- [ mv](/docs/git-mv