{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793089532625,"sessionID":"ses_e838fafdfffe3LhjKrXU2o8Kh0","part":{"partID":"prt_17c76e0c3001p2cmoUW3G26iM8","sessionID":"ses_e838fafdfffe3LhjKrXU2o8Kh0","messageID":"msg_17c76d69d001liu1PEK9nsswT3","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-973070b8009c2d46","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":2,\"run\":2,\"runId\":\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-1017-1793088864734-4s5169\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-1017-1793088864734-4s5169\",\"lineageId\":\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-1017-1793088864734-4s5169\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"newInfoRatio\":0.9,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Git 2.50.1's fsmonitor daemon lifecycle, and why a wedged daemon never recovers\",\"findingsCount\":12,\"noveltyJustification\":\"Eleven of twelve findings are new to the packet: the man-page lifecycle, the ipcthreads default, the no-op Darwin health thread, the source-admitted infinite cookie wait and the unbounded client read were all unrecorded.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Q1. What unset speckit.worktreeBase and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and does anything still create worktrees under .worktrees/ by default?\",\"Q2. What is git 2.50.1's documented fsmonitor daemon lifecycle on macOS, and how do fsmonitor.socketDir, idle shutdown and git fsmonitor--daemon stop behave when the daemon is wedged?\",\"Q3. Is event overload the real cause of the hang, or is there a known daemon deadlock in this git version, for example around --ipc-threads or the cookie-file handshake?\",\"Q4. Which call sites in the repo's hooks and scripts run git without a timeout, and which of them should opt out of fsmonitor?\",\"Q5. What is the safest default: fsmonitor on with worktrees outside the checkout, or fsmonitor off for the main checkout and on per worktree?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"Q2. What is git 2.50.1's documented fsmonitor daemon lifecycle on macOS, and how do fsmonitor.socketDir, idle shutdown and git fsmonitor--daemon stop behave when the daemon is wedged?\",\"Q3. Is event overload the real cause of the hang, or is there a known daemon deadlock in this git version, for example around --ipc-threads or the cookie-file handshake?\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"--ipc-threads=8 is a repo or Apple tuning knob and the root cause\",\"A git upgrade past 2.50.1 fixes the hang\",\"Daemons exit on their own after idle time\"],\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Bash\",\"WebFetch\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\"man git-fsmonitor--daemon\",\"man git-config\",\"builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c\",\"compat/simple-ipc/ipc-unix-socket.c\",\"compat/fsmonitor/fsm-health-darwin.c\",\"compat/fsmonitor/fsm-health.h\",\"Documentation/RelNotes/2.51.0.adoc\",\"Documentation/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc\",\"Documentation/RelNotes/2.53.0.adoc\",\"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/scratch/findings.md\"],\"edgeCase\":\"missing-dependency\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-27T08:25:08Z\",\"durationMs\":0,\"graphEvents\":[{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"q2-daemon-lifecycle\",\"kind\":\"QUESTION\",\"label\":\"Documented fsmonitor daemon lifecycle on macOS\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"q3-wedge-cause\",\"kind\":\"QUESTION\",\"label\":\"Overload versus known daemon deadlock\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-no-idle-exit\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"No idle shutdown or self-exit is documented or implemented\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-darwin-health-noop\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"The Darwin health thread is an empty stub\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-cookie-infinite-wait\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"The daemon cookie handshake is an acknowledged infinite wait\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-client-unbounded-read\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"The IPC client reply read has no deadline\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-q2-1\",\"source\":\"f-no-idle-exit\",\"target\":\"q2-daemon-lifecycle\",\"relation\":\"ANSWERS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-q2-2\",\"source\":\"f-darwin-health-noop\",\"target\":\"q2-daemon-lifecycle\",\"relation\":\"ANSWERS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-q3-1\",\"source\":\"f-cookie-infinite-wait\",\"target\":\"q3-wedge-cause\",\"relation\":\"ANSWERS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-q3-2\",\"source\":\"f-client-unbounded-read\",\"target\":\"f-cookie-infinite-wait\",\"relation\":\"SUPPORTS\"}]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter002-001\",\"label\":\"The 2.50.1 manual documents only start, run, stop and status over a single working directory, and specifies no idle timeout, lifetime bound, self-exit or TTL.\",\"iteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"man git-fsmonitor--daemon\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter002-002\",\"label\":\"--ipc-threads=8 is git's compiled default for fsmonitor.ipcthreads, not repo configuration; this checkout sets no fsmonitor.* key.\",\"iteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c:35\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter002-003\",\"label\":\"fsmonitor.starttimeout (default 60 s) is the only lifecycle timeout and bounds startup only, never a request.\",\"iteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c:38\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter002-004\",\"label\":\"On macOS the health thread is a no-op: fsm_health__ctor, fsm_health__loop and fsm_health__stop_async return immediately, so the daemon never monitors or retires itself.\",\"iteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"compat/fsmonitor/fsm-health-darwin.c:1\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter002-005\",\"label\":\"git fsmonitor--daemon stop sends quit and then polls fsmonitor_ipc__get_state every 50 ms with no deadline, so a wedged daemon makes stop hang as well.\",\"iteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c:88\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter002-006\",\"label\":\"Every non-quit query creates a cookie file inside the watched tree and then waits in an unbounded pthread_cond_wait; the source comment calls it an infinite wait and says the timed variant was not implemented.\",\"iteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c:198\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter002-007\",\"label\":\"ipc_client_send_command_to_connection reads the reply with read_packetized_to_strbuf and no poll or timeout, so only EOF or a read error releases the client; this is the exact frame in the packet's sample.\",\"iteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"compat/simple-ipc/ipc-unix-socket.c:192\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter002-008\",\"label\":\"The hang is not a two-owner lock deadlock but an unbounded wait on both sides of the socket, reachable whenever the cookie's filesystem event never reaches the daemon listener.\",\"iteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c:198\",\"compat/simple-ipc/ipc-unix-socket.c:192\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter002-009\",\"label\":\"Event overload is the trigger rather than the defect: a roughly 570k-file checkout plus roughly 2M files under .worktrees with 93 node_modules trees can lose or coalesce the cookie event, and the unbounded wait converts that into a 30-minute hang.\",\"iteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/scratch/findings.md\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter002-010\",\"label\":\"The 2.51, 2.52 and 2.53 release notes contain zero fsmonitor entries, so no announced upstream fix addresses the unbounded cookie wait.\",\"iteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"Documentation/RelNotes/2.51.0.adoc\",\"Documentation/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc\",\"Documentation/RelNotes/2.53.0.adoc\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter002-011\",\"label\":\"Since no idle exit or health exit exists, PID 17228's disappearance at 09:17:59 indicates a signal or crash rather than a timeout, with the unified log or DiagnosticReports as the resolving check.\",\"iteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/scratch/findings.md\",\"compat/fsmonitor/fsm-health-darwin.c:1\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter002-012\",\"label\":\"Each blocked client holds one of the 8 IPC workers, so a saturated pool also stops answering status and stop, which is why the whole checkout appears frozen.\",\"iteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c:35\",\"compat/simple-ipc/ipc-unix-socket.c:440\"]}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"--ipc-threads=8 is a repo or Apple tuning knob and the root cause\",\"reason\":\"8 is the compiled default of fsmonitor.ipcthreads and the repo sets no fsmonitor key.\",\"iteration\":2}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"A git upgrade past 2.50.1 fixes the hang\",\"reason\":\"Release notes for 2.51-2.53 have zero fsmonitor entries and the 2.50.1 source says the timed wait was never implemented.\",\"iteration\":2}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"Daemons exit on their own after an idle period\",\"reason\":\"No idle mechanism exists in the manual or source, and the Darwin health thread is an empty stub.\",\"iteration\":2}\n","path":"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-1017/deltas/iter-002.jsonl"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-1017/deltas/iter-002.jsonl","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-1017/deltas/iter-002.jsonl"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"{\\\"type\\\":\\\"iteration\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":2,\\\"run\\\":2,\\\"runId\\\":\\\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-1017-1793088864734-4s5169\\\",\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-1017-1793088864734-4s5169\\\",\\\"lineageId\\\":\\\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-1017-1793088864734-4s5169\\\",\\\"mode\\\":\\\"research\\\",\\\"target_agent\\\":\\\"deep-research\\\",\\\"agent_definition_loaded\\\":true,\\\"resolved_route\\\":\\\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\\\",\\\"newInfoRatio\\\":0.9,\\\"status\\\":\\\"complete\\\",\\\"focus\\\":\\\"Git 2.50.1's fsmonitor daemon lifecycle, and why a wedged daemon never recovers\\\",\\\"findingsCount\\\":12,\\\"noveltyJustification\\\":\\\"Eleven of twelve findings are new to the packet: the man-page lifecycle, the ipcthreads default, the no-op Darwin health thread, the source-admitted infinite cookie wait and the unbounded client read were all unrecorded.\\\",\\\"keyQuestions\\\":[\\\"Q1. What unset speckit.worktreeBase and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and does anything still create worktrees under .worktrees/ by default?\\\",\\\"Q2. What is git 2.50.1's documented fsmonitor daemon lifecycle on macOS, and how do fsmonitor.socketDir, idle shutdown and git fsmonitor--daemon stop behave when the daemon is wedged?\\\",\\\"Q3. Is event overload the real cause of the hang, or is there a known daemon deadlock in this git version, for example around --ipc-threads or the cookie-file handshake?\\\",\\\"Q4. Which call sites in the repo's hooks and scripts run git without a timeout, and which of them should opt out of fsmonitor?\\\",\\\"Q5. What is the safest default: fsmonitor on with worktrees outside the checkout, or fsmonitor off for the main checkout and on per worktree?\\\"],\\\"answeredQuestions\\\":[\\\"Q2. What is git 2.50.1's documented fsmonitor daemon lifecycle on macOS, and how do fsmonitor.socketDir, idle shutdown and git fsmonitor--daemon stop behave when the daemon is wedged?\\\",\\\"Q3. Is event overload the real cause of the hang, or is there a known daemon deadlock in this git version, for example around --ipc-threads or the cookie-file handshake?\\\"],\\\"ruledOut\\\":[\\\"--ipc-threads=8 is a repo or Apple tuning knob and the root cause\\\",\\\"A git upgrade past 2.50.1 fixes the hang\\\",\\\"Daemons exit on their own after idle time\\\"],\\\"toolsUsed\\\":[\\\"Read\\\",\\\"Bash\\\",\\\"WebFetch\\\"],\\\"sourcesQueried\\\":[\\\"man git-fsmonitor--daemon\\\",\\\"man git-config\\\",\\\"builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c\\\",\\\"compat/simple-ipc/ipc-unix-socket.c\\\",\\\"compat/fsmonitor/fsm-health-darwin.c\\\",\\\"compat/fsmonitor/fsm-health.h\\\",\\\"Documentation/RelNotes/2.51.0.adoc\\\",\\\"Documentation/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc\\\",\\\"Documentation/RelNotes/2.53.0.adoc\\\",\\\"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/scratch/findings.md\\\"],\\\"edgeCase\\\":\\\"missing-dependency\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-10-27T08:25:08Z\\\",\\\"durationMs\\\":0,\\\"graphEvents\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"q2-daemon-lifecycle\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"QUESTION\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Documented fsmonitor daemon lifecycle on macOS\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"q3-wedge-cause\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"QUESTION\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Overload versus known daemon deadlock\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-no-idle-exit\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"FINDING\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"No idle shutdown or self-exit is documented or implemented\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-darwin-health-noop\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"FINDING\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The Darwin health thread is an empty stub\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-cookie-infinite-wait\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"FINDING\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The daemon cookie handshake is an acknowledged infinite wait\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-client-unbounded-read\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"FINDING\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The IPC client reply read has no deadline\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"edge\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"e-q2-1\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"f-no-idle-exit\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"q2-daemon-lifecycle\\\",\\\"relation\\\":\\\"ANSWERS\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"edge\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"e-q2-2\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"f-darwin-health-noop\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"q2-daemon-lifecycle\\\",\\\"relation\\\":\\\"ANSWERS\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"edge\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"e-q3-1\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"f-cookie-infinite-wait\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"q3-wedge-cause\\\",\\\"relation\\\":\\\"ANSWERS\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"edge\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"e-q3-2\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"f-client-unbounded-read\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"f-cookie-infinite-wait\\\",\\\"relation\\\":\\\"SUPPORTS\\\"}]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter002-001\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The 2.50.1 manual documents only start, run, stop and status over a single working directory, and specifies no idle timeout, lifetime bound, self-exit or TTL.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":2,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"man git-fsmonitor--daemon\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter002-002\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"--ipc-threads=8 is git's compiled default for fsmonitor.ipcthreads, not repo configuration; this checkout sets no fsmonitor.* key.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":2,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c:35\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter002-003\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"fsmonitor.starttimeout (default 60 s) is the only lifecycle timeout and bounds startup only, never a request.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":2,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c:38\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter002-004\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"On macOS the health thread is a no-op: fsm_health__ctor, fsm_health__loop and fsm_health__stop_async return immediately, so the daemon never monitors or retires itself.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":2,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"compat/fsmonitor/fsm-health-darwin.c:1\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter002-005\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"git fsmonitor--daemon stop sends quit and then polls fsmonitor_ipc__get_state every 50 ms with no deadline, so a wedged daemon makes stop hang as well.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":2,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c:88\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter002-006\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Every non-quit query creates a cookie file inside the watched tree and then waits in an unbounded pthread_cond_wait; the source comment calls it an infinite wait and says the timed variant was not implemented.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":2,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c:198\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter002-007\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"ipc_client_send_command_to_connection reads the reply with read_packetized_to_strbuf and no poll or timeout, so only EOF or a read error releases the client; this is the exact frame in the packet's sample.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":2,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"compat/simple-ipc/ipc-unix-socket.c:192\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter002-008\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The hang is not a two-owner lock deadlock but an unbounded wait on both sides of the socket, reachable whenever the cookie's filesystem event never reaches the daemon listener.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":2,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c:198\\\",\\\"compat/simple-ipc/ipc-unix-socket.c:192\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter002-009\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Event overload is the trigger rather than the defect: a roughly 570k-file checkout plus roughly 2M files under .worktrees with 93 node_modules trees can lose or coalesce the cookie event, and the unbounded wait converts that into a 30-minute hang.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":2,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/scratch/findings.md\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter002-010\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The 2.51, 2.52 and 2.53 release notes contain zero fsmonitor entries, so no announced upstream fix addresses the unbounded cookie wait.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":2,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"Documentation/RelNotes/2.51.0.adoc\\\",\\\"Documentation/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc\\\",\\\"Documentation/RelNotes/2.53.0.adoc\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter002-011\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Since no idle exit or health exit exists, PID 17228's disappearance at 09:17:59 indicates a signal or crash rather than a timeout, with the unified log or DiagnosticReports as the resolving check.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":2,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/scratch/findings.md\\\",\\\"compat/fsmonitor/fsm-health-darwin.c:1\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter002-012\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Each blocked client holds one of the 8 IPC workers, so a saturated pool also stops answering status and stop, which is why the whole checkout appears frozen.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":2,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c:35\\\",\\\"compat/simple-ipc/ipc-unix-socket.c:440\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"ruled_out\\\",\\\"direction\\\":\\\"--ipc-threads=8 is a repo or Apple tuning knob and the root cause\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"8 is the compiled default of fsmonitor.ipcthreads and the repo sets no fsmonitor key.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":2}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"ruled_out\\\",\\\"direction\\\":\\\"A git upgrade past 2.50.1 fixes the hang\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Release notes for 2.51-2.53 have zero fsmonitor entries and the 2.50.1 source says the timed wait was never implemented.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":2}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"ruled_out\\\",\\\"direction\\\":\\\"Daemons exit on their own after an idle period\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"No idle mechanism exists in the manual or source, and the Darwin health thread is an empty stub.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":2}\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-1017/deltas/iter-002.jsonl\"}"},"time":{"start":1793089528003,"end":1793089532625}}}}
