us`, `newInfoRatio`, `ruledOut` and `timestamp`, and the gateway returned no warning field alongside `ok: true`. The delta files retain every field, which is why the reducer still resolved 5 of 5 questions and counted 33 findings; a reducer that read only the projection would have seen unanswered questions. Fix direction for the loop owner: emit the canonical `{stem, scope, data}` envelope rather than a legacy-shaped row, or have the upcaster surface a lossy-field warning. Recorded here instead of repaired, because re-appending a corrected iteration record would duplicate the iteration count.\n\n**Scope discipline.** Every write in this lineage landed inside `research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-1017`. No index-reading git command was run (only `log`, `show`, `config`, `rev-parse`), so the checkout's index and `.git/config` are untouched. `validate.sh --strict`, `generate-context.js`, `git add` staging and the `spec.md` findings write-back were **not** run: they write outside this lineage's authority, and the dispatcher's write limit outranks the workflow's default save/synthesis steps. Their content is preserved in `research.md` for the follow-up packet.\n\n**External concurrent activity.** Files under `specs/system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/` carry an mtime of 09:21:47 during this run. They are outside this lineage and were written by another process; this lineage never opened them.\n\n---\n\n## Appendix A: Convergence Report","oldString":"---\n\n## Appendix A: Convergence Report","path":"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-1017/research.md"},"output":"Edited specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-1017/research.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineage